# Project conventions

## Stack
- **Vite + vanilla TypeScript.** No React/Vue/Svelte/Angular and no heavy UI kits. Small DOM helpers in `src/lib` are fine.
- KaTeX is installed but not needed for the tracker; don't add it to new code.
- **PWA**: manifest + service worker (`vite-plugin-pwa`, `registerType: 'prompt'`). Everything works offline; no network calls at runtime.
- **Static only**: deployed to GitHub Pages (repo `xgrybvo6508-dot/reboard-ai`). Vite `base: '/reboard-ai/'`. Every asset URL, manifest `start_url`/`scope` and SW scope must respect this base. Use `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, not hard-coded `/`.
- Tooling: `vitest` + `happy-dom` + `fake-indexeddb`, `eslint` (typescript-eslint), `prettier`, `tsx`, `@playwright/test` for e2e. Node ≥ 20.19.

## Folder layout (tracker)
```
src/
  main.ts          # bootstrap only
  lib/             # pure helpers (dom, guards, ids)
  data/            # course parser + bundled course data (from learning-system/courses-v2)
  progress/        # done-mark store (versioned, migrations) + progress maths
  ui/              # views/CSS — per Vladislav's design
```
`src/agent/`, `src/memory/`, `src/modules/*` are legacy (see 05-tracker-scope): don't extend.
Tests are colocated as `*.test.ts`.

## Code style
- `tsconfig`: `"strict": true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `noImplicitOverride`. No `any`. Use `unknown` + type guards at boundaries (localStorage/IndexedDB, parsed course data).
- **Small pure modules.** Logic in `data/`, `progress/`, `lib/` is pure and DOM-free where possible so it can be unit-tested. Side effects (storage, DOM) sit behind thin adapters that get injected.
- ES modules and named exports. One responsibility per file, roughly under 200 lines.
- Persisted data has a `version` field and a migration function. Never silently drop user memory.
- Errors are typed (`Result`-style or custom `Error` subclasses) and reach the UI as calm, plain-English messages.

## Testing
- vitest covers the course parser (IDs, titles, ✅ → done), progress maths, and storage migrations.
- Fake storage; no network in tests. The stop hook (`.cursor/hooks/verify.sh`) runs typecheck + lint + tests automatically when TS changed.

## npm scripts (keep these names)
| script | command |
|---|---|
| `dev` | `vite` |
| `build` | `tsc --noEmit && vite build` |
| `preview` | `vite preview` |
| `test` | `vitest run` |
| `lint` | `eslint .` |
| `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |
| `format` | `prettier --write .` |

Before declaring work done, run: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test && npm run build`.
